{"report": {"question": "Explique como funciona proof of stake.", "mode": "react_agent", "status": "complete", "answer": "O Proof of Stake (PoS) é um mecanismo de consenso onde validadores bloqueiam (fazem stake) moedas como garantia para participar da validação da rede e receber recompensas em moeda. O comportamento malicioso pode resultar em *slashing*, que é a perda parcial do stake. Este mecanismo é usado pelo Ethereum desde 2022, enquanto o Proof of Work (PoW) é usado pelo Bitcoin.", "key_points": [], "findings": [{"statement": "Base de conhecimento: 'Ethereum e staking' (ethereum-staking.md)", "source_tool": "search_knowledge_base", "source_updated_at": null, "retrieved_at": null}, {"statement": "Base de conhecimento: 'Fundamentos de blockchain' (blockchain-basics.md)", "source_tool": "search_knowledge_base", "source_updated_at": null, "retrieved_at": null}], "data_sources": [{"provider": "base de conhecimento local (Chroma)", "tool": "search_knowledge_base", "endpoint": "crypto_knowledge", "source_updated_at": null, "retrieved_at": null}], "uncertainties": [], "tool_calls": [{"tool": "search_knowledge_base", "input": "como funciona proof of stake", "ok": true, "error_kind": null, "error_message": null}], "decision_summary": ["search_knowledge_base input=como funciona proof of stake"], "model": "gemma4:e2b", "generated_at": "2026-11-05T00:46:02.776446Z"}, "session_id": "d907581ca61d4d6c97f6d83ce93e17d0", "trace": [{"kind": "llm", "name": "llm", "detail": "input_tokens=2318 output_tokens=17", "duration_ms": 17744.57720800001, "ok": true, "at": "2026-11-05T00:45:42.744+00:00"}, {"kind": "decision", "name": "search_knowledge_base", "detail": "input=como funciona proof of stake", "duration_ms": null, "ok": null, "at": "2026-11-05T00:45:42.744+00:00"}, {"kind": "tool", "name": "search_knowledge_base", "detail": "{\"ok\": true, \"tool\": \"search_knowledge_base\", \"data\": [{\"source\": \"ethereum-staking.md\", \"title\": \"Ethereum e staking\", \"chunk_id\": \"eth